# CODEOWNERS
#
# Default owners for every path in this repository.
#
# Enforcement lives in the repository ruleset "main: require review + ci + gitleaks".
# What that ruleset actually enforces on the default branch:
#   - 1 approving review required
#   - the approval must come from a CODEOWNER (this file)
#   - stale approvals are dismissed when new commits are pushed
#   - the approval must come from someone other than the last pusher
#   - all review conversations must be resolved
#   - status checks `ci` and `gitleaks` must pass
#   - force pushes and branch deletion are blocked
#
# Two bypasses exist, both deliberate:
#   - Repository admin: so an owner can unblock the repo in an emergency.
#   - The Renovate app: dependency PRs cannot approve themselves, so without this
#     bypass every Renovate PR would wait on a human forever and automerge would
#     be dead. Renovate PRs still have to pass `ci` and `gitleaks`; they only
#     skip the review count.
#
# Reviews only count toward CODEOWNER review if the reviewer has write access.

